
                                                    ABM COMMAND


Performs ABM and BMI build

Below is the syntax :
          abm 	-primary address [-bmiprimary address] [-bmisec address] [-device]

---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES       |    DESCRIPTION
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -primary    |    Start address of ABM primary location. Mandatory switch. 
   -bmiprimary |    Start address of BMI primary location. Optional Switch.  
   -bmisec     |    Start address of BMI secondary location. Optional switch.
   -device     |    Takes value IFX_65NM, IFX_40NM, DEV5 (It is IFX_40NM DEV5), TC2XX, TC3XX. Optional field.
               |    Default value is IFX_65nm.
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example:
	1)	read -in rba_BootCtrl_hexmod.hex -igcks true
		abm -primary 0x80000999
		write -out _out/output_abm.hex -lyt 0x10		

	2)	read -in rba_BootCtrl_hexmod.hex -igcks true
		abm -primary 0x800F0000 -bmiprimary 0xAF400000 -bmisec 0xAF400200
		write -out _out/output_abm.hex -lyt 0x20		

	3)	read -in Test_TC39X.hex -igcks true
		abm -primary 0x80000000 -device IFX_40NM
		write -out _out/output_abm.hex -lyt 0x10
		
